# Content Authoring

Gate Life uses YAML files for game content definitions. All registries load at server startup.

## Adding Content

### Character Class
1. Create `class_templates/<class_id>.yaml` with required fields (see `dog_boy.yaml`)
2. Optionally create `class_templates/<class_id>_creation.yaml` for rolled creation
3. If custom creation logic is needed, add a handler in `CharacterCreationService.ts`
4. No other code changes needed — class appears in `GET /api/state/templates`

### Enemy Type
1. Create `content/enemies/<enemy_id>.yaml`
2. Required fields: `id`, `name`, `enemy_type`, `hp_max`, `apm`, `damage`, `damage_type`
3. Available via `EnemyTypeRegistry.getEnemyType(id)`

### Item
1. Create `content/items/<item_id>.yaml`
2. Required fields: `id`, `name`, `type`, `weight`, `value`, `rarity`
3. Available via `ItemRegistry.getItemTemplate(id)`

### Terrain Type
1. Create `content/terrain/<type_id>.yaml`
2. Required fields: `id`, `name`, `movement_cost`, `cover`, `elevation`, `tile_color`
3. Available via `TerrainTypeRegistry.getTerrainType(id)`

### Entity Type
1. Create `content/entity-types/<type_id>.yaml`
2. Required fields: `id`, `label`, `icon`, `spawn_as`, `hostile`
3. Also add to `ScenarioEntityType` union in `packages/shared/src/types.ts`

## Conventions
- File names use snake_case matching the `id` field
- All YAML files must have a top-level `id` field
- Use existing files as templates when creating new content
- Restart server after adding/modifying YAML files
